[{"id":4891354089,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI4wj6Q","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"276c5b2406dd18ca0ef2776eab35eb76c5ed7b6f","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"Looks nice!\n\nTwo comments to your benchmark: Some of those aren't very representative (measure ideal conditions instead of a realistic workload); i saw you had GDScript tests but scrapped them due to high variance. That's around what I'd expect to see since other costs likely outweigh this one.\n\nEspecially notable: The hashmap lookup is probably mostly bottlenecked by cache misses (cold lookups); hot hashmap lookups I would expect to be quite rare. It's hard to test this, but anyway your PR doesn't change this so it's not a regression.\n\nOverall i think this is a nice improvement and it matches my understanding of what bottlenecks the hot path, and it looks correct so I think this is mergable.\n\nJust two stylistic notes.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121342#pullrequestreview-4891354089","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121342","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-08-09T13:08:47Z"},{"id":4892727380,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI6EYVA","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"276c5b2406dd18ca0ef2776eab35eb76c5ed7b6f","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12262539?u=7589c86a57a21eb6ee97337c423069e53dd3b1a1&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"